{title: Shenandoah}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}
{meta: public_domain Traditional American folk song and sea shanty, sung from the early 19th century.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh [D]Shenandoah, I [G]long to [D]see you,
A[D]way, you [Bm]rolling [G]river,
Oh [D]Shenandoah, I [Bm]long to [A]see you,
A[G]way, I'm [D]bound a[Bm]way, 'cross the [A]wide Mis[D]souri.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh [D]Shenandoah, I [G]love your [D]daughter,
A[D]way, you [Bm]rolling [G]river,
For [D]her I'd cross your [Bm]roaming [A]waters,
A[G]way, I'm [D]bound a[Bm]way, 'cross the [A]wide Mis[D]souri.
{end_of_verse}
